-- title:
--   Atkin–Lehner automorphism wₚ of ℚ̄(X₁(Mp))
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M\ge 1$ with $p\nmid M$; let $y,w_0\in\mathbb Z$ satisfy $pw_0-My=1$, let $\gamma,\gamma'\in\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ be the matrices $\begin{pmatrix}1&y\\ M&pw_0\end{pmatrix}$ and $\begin{pmatrix}w_0&-y\\ -M&p\end{pmatrix}$, and let $\iota\colon\overline{\mathbb Q}\to\mathbb C$ be a ring homomorphism. Write $F$ for `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`, the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the coefficientwise image of $\mathbb Q$-subfield `x1FunctionField (M * p)` of $\mathbb Q((q))$, and let $\iota_*$ denote the coefficientwise map $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))\to\mathbb C((q))$ induced by $\iota$. The assertion is that there is a $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $F$ with four properties. First, every $x\in F$ has a presentation: there are a weight $k$ and modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ with the $q$-expansion of $g$ (width $1$, viewed as a Laurent series) nonzero, $\iota_*x$ equal to the quotient of the $q$-expansions of $f$ and $g$, and each of the four functions $z\mapsto (h\mid_k\delta)(\,!![p,0;0,1]\cdot z)$, for $h\in\{f,g\}$ and $\delta\in\{\gamma,\gamma'\}$, equal to $1/D$ times a weight-$k$ form on $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ for some nonzero integer $D$. Second, whenever $x$ is so presented by $f,g$ and $\varphi,\psi$ are weight-$k$ forms on $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ with $\varphi=D\cdot (f\mid_k\gamma)(p\,\cdot)$, $\psi=E\cdot (g\mid_k\gamma)(p\,\cdot)$, $D,E\ne 0$, then $\iota_*(\tau x)$ equals the constant $E/D$ times the quotient of the $q$-expansions of $\varphi$ and $\psi$. Third, the same law with $\gamma$ replaced by $\gamma'$ computes $\iota_*(\tau^{-1}x)$. Fourth, if $j\in F$ has underlying Laurent series the image of the rational $j$-series `jq` under the coefficient embedding, then $\tau j$ has underlying series the image of `qExpand ℚ p jq`, i.e. of $j$ with $q$ replaced by $q^p$.
--
--   This is the partial Atkin–Lehner operator $W_p=\gamma\,\mathrm{diag}(p,1)$ realised as an automorphism of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, characterised analytically by transport of quotients of modular forms through a fixed complex embedding. It is obtained from the general slash-transport construction together with the decomposition of $(f\mid_k\gamma)(p\,\cdot)$ into integral forms on $\Gamma_1(Mp)$, and it feeds the comparison of $\tau$ with diamond operators and the construction of the full Atkin–Lehner involution.
